statement:
In the setup of [def-weil-pbc-strict-henselian-setup]: let $(A,\mathfrak m)$ be a strictly henselian local ring with residue field $\kappa=A/\mathfrak m$, $S=\operatorname{Spec}A$, $s=\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, $X=\mathbf P^1_S=\mathbf P(\{0,1\};S)$ [def-nagata-projective-space-base-change], $X_0=\mathbf P^1_s=X\times_Ss$ its closed fibre and $i:X_0\to X$ the closed immersion (the base change of $s\to S$). Let $r$ be a prime and $I$ an injective object [def-sp-injective-resolutions] of the abelian category $\Mod(X_{\Et},\mathbf F_r)$ of sheaves of $\mathbf F_r$-modules on $X_{\Et}$ [def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category], [def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves]; write $i^{-1}$ for the inverse image of sheaves of $\mathbf F_r$-modules [def-weil-pbc-inverse-image]. For a morphism $\varphi$ of sheaves of $\mathbf F_r$-modules on $X_0$ write $H^1(\varphi)$ for the induced map on the etale cohomology [def-weil-pbc-etale-cohomology] of the underlying abelian sheaves [lem-weil-pbc-cohomology-pullback-functorial]. Then for every class $\xi\in H^1(X_{0,\Et},i^{-1}I)$ there are an integer $n\ge0$ and, for $j=1,\dots,n$:
- a finite morphism $h_j:V_j\to X$ [def-weil-finite-integral-morphism] which is locally of finite presentation [def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation];
- a finite $\mathbf F_r$-module $M_j$, with constant sheaf of $\mathbf F_r$-modules $\underline{M_j}$ on $V_{j,\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf] and direct image $(h_j)_*\underline{M_j}\in\Mod(X_{\Et},\mathbf F_r)$ [def-weil-pbc-direct-image];
- a morphism $\psi_j:(h_j)_*\underline{M_j}\to I$ of sheaves of $\mathbf F_r$-modules;
- a class $x_j\in H^1(X_{0,\Et},i^{-1}(h_j)_*\underline{M_j})$,
such that
$$\xi=\sum_{j=1}^nH^1(i^{-1}\psi_j)(x_j).$$
(This is the form of the Lean statement AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.exists_sum_eq_of_injective_projectiveLine; equivalently $\xi$ is the image of a class of $H^1(X_0,i^{-1}\bigoplus_j(h_j)_*\underline{M_j})$ under $i^{-1}$ of a map $\bigoplus_j(h_j)_*\underline{M_j}\to I$. Remark: the proof uses only that $X$ and $X_0$ are quasi-compact and quasi-separated, not that $A$ is henselian; the hypothesis is kept as in the setup and the Lean declaration.)
